salesforce_training Day-18

1.System Overview
-> The system is a College Management System built on Salesforce that manages students, courses, faculty, attendance, fees, and approvals using Flows, Apex, LWC, and AI assistance.
Key Modules
* Student Management
* Course Management
* Faculty Management
* Attendance Tracking
* Fee Management
* Approval Workflows
* AI Assistance (Agentforce)
The system is designed for scalability, automation, and enterprise-grade governance.

2.Architecture Overview
-> The system follows a layered architecture model.
Layers
1. Frontend Layer
* Lightning Web Components (LWC)
* User Interface
* Data display and interaction
 Business Logic Layer
* Flows
* Apex Classes
* Validation Rules
3. Data Layer
* Salesforce Objects
* Relationships
* Data Storage
4. Integration Layer
* APIs
* External systems
* AI services
This separation ensures modular and maintainable design.

3.Objects & Relationships
-> Salesforce objects represent real-world entities.
Objects
* Student__c
* Course__c
* Faculty__c
* Attendance__c
* Fee__c
* Enrollment__c
Relationships
* Student → Enrollment (One-to-Many)
* Course → Enrollment (One-to-Many)
* Faculty → Course (One-to-Many)
* Student → Attendance (One-to-Many)
Relationships ensure structured and connected data.

4.Validation Rules
-> Validation rules ensure data accuracy and consistency.
Examples
* Student Email must be valid format
* Fee Amount cannot be negative
* Attendance cannot exceed 100%
* Mandatory fields must be filled
Benefits
* Prevents incorrect data entry
* Maintains data integrity
* Improves reporting accuracy
* Reduces errors
Validation rules enforce business correctness.

5.Flow Explanations
-> Flows automate business processes without code.
Examples
1. Enrollment Flow
* Student applies for course
* System checks availability
* Auto-enroll or waitlist
 Fee Approval Flow
* Student submits payment request
* Manager approval required
* Finance verification
* Confirmation generated
Flows reduce manual effort and improve efficiency.
6.Apex Logic
-> Apex is used for complex business logic.
Examples
* Bulk fee calculation
* Automated attendance processing
* Trigger-based record updates
* Integration with external APIs
Benefits
* Handles complex logic
* Supports bulk operations
* Enables automation beyond Flow limits
Apex provides powerful backend processing.

7.LWC Screens
-> Lightning Web Components provide the user interface.
Screens
* Student Dashboard
* Course Registration Screen
* Fee Payment Screen
* Attendance View
* Admin Control Panel
Benefits
* Fast UI rendering
* Reusable components
* Interactive experience
* Real-time updates
LWC improves user experience and performance.

8.Workflow Explanation
-> The system follows a structured workflow.
1. User submits request (UI - LWC)
2. Flow validates input
3. Apex executes business logic
4. Data stored in Salesforce objects
5. Approval process triggered if required
6. AI agent provides suggestions
7. Final status updated
This ensures smooth end-to-end automation.
Scaling Considerations
-> Enterprise systems must handle growth and performance.
Challenges
* Large number of users
* High data volume
* Concurrent transactions
* API limits
* Performance bottlenecks
Solutions
* Use bulk processing in Apex
* Optimize SOQL queries
* Use asynchronous processing
* Modular architecture
* Efficient data modeling
Scalability ensures system reliability under heavy load.

Revised Question and Answers:

1. Why do enterprise systems require layered architecture?
-> Layered architecture separates responsibilities into UI, logic, and data layers to improve maintainability, scalability, and flexibility.
2. Why are frontend/backend separation important?
-> Separation allows independent development, easier debugging, and better system organization.
3. Why are Flows and Apex both useful?
-> Flows handle simple automation while Apex handles complex business logic.
4. Why are reusable components powerful?
-> Reusable components reduce duplication, improve consistency, and speed up development.
5. Why do enterprise systems require approvals?
-> Approvals ensure control, accountability, and validation of critical business actions.
6. Why is debugging important?
-> Debugging helps identify, analyze, and fix system issues quickly.
7. Why is data quality critical?
-> Data quality ensures accurate reporting, reliable decisions, and system integrity.
8. Why do large systems require scalability thinking?
-> Scalability ensures the system performs efficiently under increased load.
9. How can AI improve enterprise systems?
-> AI improves automation, decision-making, predictions, and user experience.
10. What is the difference between coding and enterprise engineering
-> Coding focuses on writing functionality, while enterprise engineering focuses on building scalable, secure, and maintainable systems with governance, testing, and architecture.
